; demand_key_tc_witness -- the @demand ACTIVATION-EQUIVALENCE witness
; (RP-6, session 6; formerly region_declared_tc_witness, the R3a bracket
; no-op-overlay witness). The pragma `@demand(From)` FORCE-ACTIVATES the
; demand transform FLAGLESS (no .drflags), declaring exactly the
; SIP-inferred key. Referees: stdout / oracle / monotone / df.opt / rel.opt
; / ir.opt / h.opt / region x4 goldens are committed SYMLINKS to
; demand_tc_witness's (which compiles under `-demand` via ITS .drflags) --
; byte-identity across every surface IS the check that pragma activation
; and flag activation produce the IDENTICAL compile. NEVER bless THIS
; case's symlinked surfaces directly (bless writes through to demand_tc's
; goldens). contract.opt is this case's OWN real golden (the
; declared-demand-key line); behavioral.stdout is ALSO real (the CBF header
; embeds the case name). NO .eqgate: the TC shape is RECURSIVE, so the
; nested arm draws the demand_cyclic_1 fence under -demand-instance.

#message edge_2(u64 From, u64 To).

#local path(u64 From, u64 To) @demand(From).
path(F, T) : edge_2(F, T).
path(F, T) : path(F, M), edge_2(M, T).

#query reachable_from(bound u64 From, free u64 To) : path(From, To).
